<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatahillah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1570</span> · Also known as Faletehan, Falatehan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fatahillah was a Muslim commander in the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demak-sultanate">Sultanate of Demak</a> who led the forces of Demak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a> and, in 1527, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-kelapa">Sunda Kalapa</a>, defeating a Portuguese landing party. He renamed the port <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jakarta">Jayakarta</a>, and Jakarta dates its founding to 22 June 1527. His identity with the Cirebon saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunan-gunung-jati">Sunan Gunung Jati</a> is debated.</p></div>
